## Results

Snapshot of one year of daily prices (Aug 2025 to Aug 2026, about 252 trading days per ticker). Volatility is the average 7-day rolling standard deviation of daily returns. The live dashboard updates with newer data, so its numbers differ slightly.

### Sector volatility vs. benchmarks

| Ticker | Group | Avg daily return | Avg volatility |
|---|---|---|---|
| QBTS | Quantum | 0.32% | 6.50% |
| RGTI | Quantum | 0.27% | 6.20% |
| QUBT | Quantum | -0.02% | 6.11% |
| IONQ | Quantum | 0.22% | 5.59% |
| QTUM | Benchmark | 0.22% | 1.88% |
| SPY | Benchmark | 0.08% | 0.76% |

The four quantum stocks are roughly 7 to 8 times as volatile as the S&P 500 (SPY) and about 3 times as volatile as the sector ETF (QTUM).

![7-day rolling volatility](volatility_chart.png)

### The stocks move together

Pairwise correlations between the four quantum stocks range from about 0.77 to 0.92. Holding two of them adds little diversification, because they tend to rise and fall on the same days.

### Forecast

An ARIMA model fit to IONQ's closing price chose a random-walk structure: the best forecast for any future day is the last observed price. The useful output is the uncertainty, not the prediction. The 95% interval widens from about $38.6 to $50.2 on day 1 to about $13.8 to $75.1 on day 30. This is descriptive, not a trading signal.

### Quantum vs. classical portfolio selection

The module picks 2 of the 4 quantum stocks by minimizing risk minus expected return, and compares QAOA (simulated with Qiskit) against an exact classical solver.

- On the full year, both methods picked IONQ and QBTS.
- With an 80/20 train/test split, both methods picked IONQ and RGTI.
- On the held-out 20%, the selected pair grew $1 to about $0.71, versus about $0.74 for an equal-weight hold of all four. The whole sector declined in that window, and the optimizer's pick did not beat the naive baseline.

QAOA matching the classical optimum is expected at this size (4 qubits, 6 possible pairs) and is not evidence of a quantum advantage. This is one split over a short window, so it should not be over-read.

### Data quality

The validation layer flagged 14 single-day price moves above 20%, all in the quantum stocks and none in the benchmarks. A typo in a benchmark `sector` label was also caught during analysis and corrected.

