## Database Schema

```text
tickers          (ticker PK, company_name, sector, is_benchmark)
daily_prices     (id PK, ticker FK, price_date, open, high, low, close, adj_close, volume)
data_quality_log (id PK, ticker FK, price_date, issue_type, note, resolved)
```

`daily_prices` and `data_quality_log` both enforce uniqueness constraints, so the pipeline can run every day without creating duplicate rows.

---

## Data Validation

Daily market data is checked before it is trusted. Price movements greater than **20% in a single day** are flagged and logged to an audit-trail table for review, instead of being silently accepted.

---

## Limitations

- Quantum computing companies have short trading histories.
- Forecasts are descriptive and are not trading signals.
- With only four assets, classical optimization matches or beats QAOA.
- The database runs on a free tier that powers off after inactivity. Scheduled runs or the dashboard can fail until it is restarted.
- Educational and portfolio project, not investment advice.

